# netsurf: Vita hardware-test diagnostics (frontends/vita)
# Generated 2026-09-22
#
# Everything a first device run needs to report back, written to
# ux0:data/VitaBrowser/ (vita/diag.c): a timestamped, crash-safe log of each
# init stage, per-page load / first-frame / CPU+GPU frame times and draw-call
# counts, free memory per pool, PGF font metrics, an allocate-until-failure
# memory probe, and plot-stream dumps in the nsmonkey format (plot.c tees
# every plotter call when a dump is open) so device renders diff against the
# host simulator's. main.c: SQUARE runs an autotest over every bundled page
# (settle, dump, dump the scrolled bottom of long pages, then font metrics
# and the probe); SELECT dumps one page, TRIANGLE probes, CIRCLE toggles a
# HUD; start-up failures are shown on screen instead of exiting silently.
# Adds the VT-* hardware test pages to the page list, LiveArea assets
# (8-bit paletted PNGs) and package-vita knobs for the ATTRIBUTE2=12
# extended-memory variant. See docs/phase-0/10-hardware-test-plan.md.

